log.\n- ✏️ **Editable & revisable** — fi"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"x a card by hand in the reader, or let an agent submit a **revised copy** (`memory_revise`); the que"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"ue labels it a revision, and an approved card is only overwritten when you approve it.\n- 🧾 **Token l"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"edger** — see how much recall injected, how many distillation calls ran, and how often recall was ac"},{"id":"p7s6","text":"tually useful.\n- 🏠 **Local-first, no cloud** — SQLite + Markdown on your own disk. No third-party me"},{"id":"p7s7","text":"mory framework, no account. Memory data never leaves the machine; only the News page fetches public "},{"id":"p7s8","text":"RSS / Hacker News on demand (titles, excerpts and outbound links only).\n- ⭐ **Core memory** — promot"},{"id":"p7s9","text":"e approved cards to always-on memory; every session gets them automatically, and the review queue st"},{"id":"p7s10","text":"ill decides what qualifies.\n- 🧭 **Reader & layout** — clickable table of contents in the card reader"},{"id":"p7s11","text":", plus a compact / normal / large layout setting for the whole memory UI."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"⭐ If it saves you from explaining the same context again, a star helps a lot.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## ⚡ Quick start"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"**DeepSeek Harness (desktop / web)**"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"**Claude Code, Codex or Cursor — same vault via MCP**"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"**Any MCP client**（MengBot / OpenClaw / Hermes 见 docs/INTEGRATIONS.md）"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"**Browser or terminal**"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## 🧬 How memory actually flows"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"One SQLite vault, one write gate, two read paths. Nothing enters recall without passing the gate."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"The diagram is only true because three invariants are enforced in code, not by convention:"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"| Invariant | Enforced by |"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"| The main store **only** ever contains approved cards | Two physical tables; every read path querie"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"s the main one |\n| An agent can never approve its own memory | Agent writes land in quarantine; appr"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"ove/reject is a human action in the UI / TUI / CLI |\n| Recall costs **zero model calls** | FTS5 + BM"},{"id":"p23s4","text":"25; the LLM runs only while distilling |"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"## 🔌 How agents talk to the memory"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"| Channel | Direction | When | Gate | Cost |"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"| `memory_recall` | agent → memory | on demand | approved only | **0 model calls** (p50 2.3 ms) |\n| "},{"id":"p26s2","text":"Core memory | memory → agent | every session, automatic | approved only | ~0.2k chars |\n| Session ca"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"pture / `memory_write` | conversation → memory | turn end | **queued for review** | 1 LLM call |\n| `"},{"id":"p26s4","text":"memory_revise` | agent → memory | on demand | **queued as a revision** | 0 |\n| Review (Web UI · TUI "},{"id":"p26s5","text":"· CLI) | human → memory | manual | — | 0 |\n| Hooks (Claude Code / Codex / Cursor) | host → memory | "},{"id":"p26s6","text":"session end | **queued** | 1 LLM call |\n| MCP server | any MCP client | on demand | same gate | same"},{"id":"p26s7","text":" |\n| News follows | web → memory | interval / 24h | isolated from cards | network only |"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## 🧾 Does it actually save tokens?"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"Most memory products say they save tokens. We think you should check. The plugin ships a built-in **"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"memory ledger** (Runtime status → Memory ledger) that records:"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"| Recorded | What it means |"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"| recall: hits + injected characters | how much memory actually entered the context |\n| capture: LLM"},{"id":"p30s2","text":" calls + input/output characters | what distillation cost you |\n| usefulness: useful / not-useful fe"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"edback | whether recalled memories actually helped |"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"The honest math:"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"| Scenario | You pay | You avoid |"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"| Multi-session project with decisions and pitfalls | ~0.6–0.9k tokens per recall | re-explaining co"},{"id":"p34s2","text":"ntext (~1.5–3k) or re-reading files (3–6k) |\n| One-off question, low hit rate | recall injection | u"},{"id":"p34s3","text":"or re-reading files (3–6k) |\n| One-off question, low hit rate | recall injection | usually nothing |"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"> Illustrative numbers, not a benchmark — measure your own with the ledger. If recall usefulness sta"},{"id":"p35s2","text":"ys below ~60%, tune it down (fewer results, shorter summaries) or turn memory off."},{"id":"p36s1","text":"## 📊 How it compares — measured on a real vault"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"Snapshot **2026-11-07**. Our figures are measured on a real **2,321-card vault** on Windows (not a t"},{"id":"p37s2","text":"oy corpus); competitor facts come from their public README / docs / license page on the same date. `"},{"id":"p37s3","text":"—` means *not advertised or not verifiable*, not \"absent\"."},{"id":"p38s1","text":"| Capability | **memory-eternal v0.25.0** | agentmemory v0.9.32 | mem0 v3 | Obsidian | CLAUDE.md / A"},{"id":"p38s2","text":"ty | **memory-eternal v0.25.0** | agentmemory v0.9.32 | mem0 v3 | Obsidian | CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md |"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"| Form factor | DSH-native plugin: capture, review UI, graph, CLI/TUI/MCP | local memory server + MC"},{"id":"p39s2","text":"P for coding agents | memory SDK / self-hosted server / cloud | local Markdown notes app | hand-writ"},{"id":"p39s3","text":"ten context files |\n| Storage | SQLite + Markdown mirror (git-friendly) | local file store (Redis op"},{"id":"p39s4","text":"tional) | vector + graph stores (self-hosted or cloud) | Markdown files on disk | one flat file |\n| "},{"id":"p39s5","text":"Write gate | **human review queue** (three stores) | automatic capture, no review | LLM extraction, "},{"id":"p39s6","text":"no review | human-written only | none |\n| Immutable audit log | ✅ enforced at the SQLite layer | ope"},{"id":"p39s7","text":"ration audit tool, not storage-enforced | — | — | — |\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
